1
00:00:01,460 --> 00:00:03,220
Well, it's about time.

2
00:00:03,660 --> 00:00:06,900
I knew that if I tormented
these children long enough,

3
00:00:07,100 --> 00:00:10,041
you'd emerge from your
musty hole sooner or later.

4
00:00:11,140 --> 00:00:11,970
Hmph.

5
00:00:12,053 --> 00:00:13,317
Time has been kind to you.

6
00:00:13,400 --> 00:00:16,677
If I didn't know better, you
could almost pass for human.

7
00:00:16,760 --> 00:00:19,100
My, my, how cavalier you've become.

8
00:00:19,340 --> 00:00:22,777
You were nothing like this the
last time I saw you, little one.

9
00:00:22,860 --> 00:00:24,120
You were so timid.

10
00:00:24,340 --> 00:00:27,164
Why, when you stood before
me two centuries ago,

11
00:00:27,380 --> 00:00:29,498
your teeth couldn't stop chattering.

12
00:00:29,860 --> 00:00:31,820
Remember, Lycerus?

13
00:00:31,980 --> 00:00:34,215
Do not call me by that name, Quinella.

14
00:00:34,420 --> 00:00:36,120
My name is Cardinal.

15
00:00:36,480 --> 00:00:40,200
I am a program with one
directive, deleting you.

16
00:00:41,460 --> 00:00:42,960
That's right, you are.

17
00:00:43,320 --> 00:00:48,860
However, my name is Administrator, and
my directive is to manage all programs.

18
00:00:49,520 --> 00:00:52,460
I'm sorry it took so long
for us to meet again?

19
00:00:52,660 --> 00:00:56,417
But you see, I was preparing
a special art to welcome you!

20
00:00:56,500 --> 00:00:59,280
and finishing it took
longer than expected.

21
00:01:14,100 --> 00:01:14,980
Damn you!

22
00:01:15,400 --> 00:01:17,180
You cut the address loose!

23
00:01:17,420 --> 00:01:22,777
I came so close to killing you 200 years
ago, but I let you slip through my fingers?

24
00:01:22,860 --> 00:01:26,100
and I wanted to make sure
that didn't happen again.

25
00:01:28,220 --> 00:01:31,640
So, I learned from my mistake
and came up with a plan.

26
00:01:31,920 --> 00:01:36,840
All I had to do was lure you out again
and trap you on this side, with me.

27
00:01:37,720 --> 00:01:40,520
Like a mouse in the same cage with a cat.

28
00:01:40,760 --> 00:01:44,701
At this point, it is not clear who
is the mouse and who is the cat.

29
00:01:44,820 --> 00:01:46,740
You are trapped in here as well.

30
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:52,180
And as you can plainly see, there
are four of us, and only one of you.

31
00:01:52,580 --> 00:01:54,137
Four against one, you say?

32
00:01:54,220 --> 00:01:55,260
Hardly.

33
00:01:55,460 --> 00:01:58,540
Your numbers are off by a
wide margin, little one.

34
00:02:02,540 --> 00:02:03,370
What?

35
00:02:06,800 --> 00:02:10,240
In fact, and this does not
include myself, mind you,

36
00:02:10,500 --> 00:02:12,382
it's four against three hundred.

37
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:14,100
Three hundred? What?

38
00:02:20,040 --> 00:02:24,100
You vile monster, is there
no limit to your depravity?

39
00:02:24,380 --> 00:02:28,262
Your duty is to protect your
subjects and you turn them into that?

40
00:02:28,540 --> 00:02:30,100
Wait, subjects?

41
00:02:30,420 --> 00:02:31,460
That thing?

42
00:02:31,780 --> 00:02:35,240
Then, that monster at
its core, this human?

43
00:02:35,660 --> 00:02:40,880
You say such silly things about trifles
such as duties and subjects to protect.

44
00:02:42,060 --> 00:02:43,820
I am a conqueror.

45
00:02:44,100 --> 00:02:46,877
I have no problem as
long as whatever I rule

46
00:02:46,960 --> 00:02:49,740
over remains subservient
and obeys my will.

47
00:02:50,440 --> 00:02:53,660
Whether they be sword or
human matters not to me.

48
00:02:54,780 --> 00:02:56,317
You horrid! Oh,

49
00:02:56,400 --> 00:02:58,697
now don't tell me you're
shocked that I used a

50
00:02:58,780 --> 00:03:01,780
little thing like matter
conversion on human units.

51
00:03:01,880 --> 00:03:04,480
It was only a measly 300 or so.

52
00:03:04,720 --> 00:03:05,980
You are evil.

53
00:03:07,180 --> 00:03:09,920
This one is just a prototype, by the way.

54
00:03:10,500 --> 00:03:13,037
In order to mass-produce the final version

55
00:03:13,120 --> 00:03:15,577
in sufficient numbers
to handle the load test,

56
00:03:15,660 --> 00:03:17,557
I expect I will need...

57
00:03:17,640 --> 00:03:20,480
oh, about half. Half? Of what?

58
00:03:21,340 --> 00:03:26,180
Why, naturally, of the 80,000 human
units living in the Human Empire.

59
00:03:26,560 --> 00:03:29,089
Yes, that amount should
be enough, I think.

60
00:03:29,380 --> 00:03:34,300
To repel the armies of the Dark Territory
and take the fight back to their side.

61
00:03:36,920 --> 00:03:40,537
Well I hope that allays
your fears, little Alice.

62
00:03:40,620 --> 00:03:46,977
Your precious human empire will be
more than protected, Madam Pontifex.

63
00:03:47,060 --> 00:03:49,937
It is clear my words cannot reach you now.

64
00:03:50,020 --> 00:03:53,657
Therefore, as a fellow sacred arts user,

65
00:03:53,740 --> 00:03:56,997
I would like to know
where the owners are of

66
00:03:57,080 --> 00:03:59,727
the 30 swords you
fashioned that monstrosity?

67
00:04:00,340 --> 00:04:01,170
out of.

68
00:04:01,253 --> 00:04:05,080
Even if you flouted the rule allowing
perfect control over one weapon,

69
00:04:05,520 --> 00:04:08,980
Pontifex or no, you cannot
break the next rule.

70
00:04:09,460 --> 00:04:13,360
To activate memory release,
there must be a bond

71
00:04:14,480 --> 00:04:16,157
between the weapon and its owner.

72
00:04:16,240 --> 00:04:17,070
Pontifex,

73
00:04:17,220 --> 00:04:19,997
if you truly used innocent humans as the

74
00:04:20,080 --> 00:04:22,417
source of the blades
which make up that thing,

75
00:04:22,500 --> 00:04:25,180
there is no way they
would form a bond with

76
00:04:27,220 --> 00:04:28,050
you!

77
00:04:28,133 --> 00:04:30,877
The explanation is hiding
in plain sight, my dear.

78
00:04:30,960 --> 00:04:33,840
Eugeo seems to have already discovered it.

79
00:04:42,780 --> 00:04:43,610
No!

80
00:04:43,693 --> 00:04:44,523
No!

81
00:04:44,606 --> 00:04:45,436
What?

82
00:04:45,519 --> 00:04:47,180
See the crystals on the ceiling?

83
00:04:47,620 --> 00:04:49,317
They're not decorations.

84
00:04:49,400 --> 00:04:53,077
They're what she stole from the
Knights with the Synthesis Ritual.

85
00:04:53,160 --> 00:04:54,631
Those are their memories!

86
00:04:56,640 --> 00:04:57,934
Curse you, Queen Ella!

87
00:04:58,400 --> 00:04:59,230
You fiend!

88
00:04:59,560 --> 00:05:02,560
Toying like this with the
humans is beyond twisted!

89
00:05:02,800 --> 00:05:07,624
You placed the memory fragments you stole
into mental models on fresh light cubes.

90
00:05:07,900 --> 00:05:11,660
That is all it would take to
create simulated human beings.

91
00:05:11,880 --> 00:05:14,477
But their intelligence
would be severely limited,

92
00:05:14,560 --> 00:05:18,240
and they would not be able to
execute an advanced command?

93
00:05:18,520 --> 00:05:20,400
such as perfect weapon control.

94
00:05:21,360 --> 00:05:24,477
But you can get around that
if the memory fragment and

95
00:05:24,560 --> 00:05:27,957
the weapon it is linked to
share the same structural data.

96
00:05:28,040 --> 00:05:30,981
The memories of people the
knights once held dear.

97
00:05:31,160 --> 00:05:34,336
The memories you stole and
carved onto these crystals.

98
00:05:34,420 --> 00:05:36,377
They are what your golem is made of.

99
00:05:36,460 --> 00:05:37,460
Isn't that right?

100
00:05:41,660 --> 00:05:45,040
These artificial personas
desire but one thing.

101
00:05:45,400 --> 00:05:50,540
To find the one they remember,
touch them, hold them, possess them.

102
00:05:51,280 --> 00:05:55,692
Unseemly desire courses throughout this
puppet and provides its motivation.

103
00:05:56,060 --> 00:05:59,877
They sense the ones they remember
are near, but they cannot touch them.

104
00:05:59,960 --> 00:06:01,666
They cannot be one with them.

105
00:06:02,180 --> 00:06:05,657
Their thirst for that connection
drives them to the point of madness.

106
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:09,780
But all they can see now are the
enemies standing in their way.

107
00:06:10,460 --> 00:06:14,872
They think if they can destroy you,
the one they desire will become theirs.

108
00:06:15,040 --> 00:06:16,077
That is why they fight.

109
00:06:16,160 --> 00:06:20,360
And no matter how badly they're
wounded, or how many times they fall,

110
00:06:20,580 --> 00:06:22,597
they'll keep fighting for eternity.

111
00:06:22,680 --> 00:06:25,040
I designed it rather well, did I not?

112
00:06:25,300 --> 00:06:29,241
The power of desire can achieve
great things if harnessed properly.

113
00:06:32,080 --> 00:06:33,240
You're wrong!

114
00:06:33,620 --> 00:06:36,973
Don't you dare tarnish that
emotion by calling it desire!

115
00:06:37,580 --> 00:06:39,617
What they feel is...

116
00:06:39,700 --> 00:06:41,500
is pure love!

117
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:45,060
Well, now you're just
splitting hairs, little one.

118
00:06:47,980 --> 00:06:49,397
Love is control.

119
00:06:49,480 --> 00:06:51,137
Love is desire.

120
00:06:51,220 --> 00:06:55,580
Either way, it is a signal produced
by a Fluctlight, nothing more.

121
00:06:56,520 --> 00:06:59,540
Which brings us to an
even greater revelation.

122
00:07:01,720 --> 00:07:08,020
Now that you know the truth about my
fearsome puppet, you cannot destroy it.

123
00:07:08,700 --> 00:07:12,377
Because every single
blade is a living human

124
00:07:12,460 --> 00:07:15,340
being who has been
transformed into a sword.

125
00:07:20,940 --> 00:07:22,857
Yes, you're right.

126
00:07:22,940 --> 00:07:24,780
I cannot kill a human.

127
00:07:25,460 --> 00:07:31,277
I spent the past 200 years owning an
art to kill you and your inhuman form,

128
00:07:31,360 --> 00:07:34,260
but it was all for nothing.

129
00:07:36,840 --> 00:07:38,520
You are such a fool!

130
00:07:38,960 --> 00:07:40,660
It's both funny and tragic.

131
00:07:41,320 --> 00:07:43,937
You knew that all life
in this world was just

132
00:07:44,020 --> 00:07:46,177
a collection of data
that can be rewritten,

133
00:07:46,260 --> 00:07:48,200
and yet you treat it as human.

134
00:07:48,580 --> 00:07:51,100
I did, because they are human.

135
00:07:51,700 --> 00:07:56,000
The people of the Underworld have the
emotions you and I lost, Quinella.

136
00:07:56,580 --> 00:08:00,940
They can laugh, grieve,
feel joy, and love.

137
00:08:01,760 --> 00:08:03,960
That is what makes them human.

138
00:08:12,260 --> 00:08:14,280
I will let you take my life!

139
00:08:14,520 --> 00:08:18,600
But first, I want your word that
you will spare these young ones!

140
00:08:18,780 --> 00:08:19,880
No, you can't!

141
00:08:23,460 --> 00:08:27,120
Out of curiosity, let us
say I accepted your offer.

142
00:08:27,340 --> 00:08:29,399
What would I stand to gain from it?

143
00:08:30,020 --> 00:08:34,460
If you decide to fight, I will not
only keep your pathetic puppet at bay,

144
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:37,717
I will shave off at least
half of your life as well.

145
00:08:37,800 --> 00:08:40,397
The loss of that would put an even greater

146
00:08:40,480 --> 00:08:43,420
strain on your already
dwindling memory capacity,

147
00:08:43,760 --> 00:08:44,760
would it not?

148
00:08:45,540 --> 00:08:46,370
Hmm.

149
00:08:48,180 --> 00:08:49,200
Very well, then.

150
00:08:52,580 --> 00:08:56,345
Letting them go now gives me
something to look forward to later.

151
00:08:57,040 --> 00:09:02,820
All right, I swear on the goddess
Stacia, after I kill - No, not on a god.

152
00:09:03,060 --> 00:09:05,457
You'll swear on the one
thing you value most.

153
00:09:05,540 --> 00:09:07,920
Your Fluctlight, or the deal is off.

154
00:09:08,340 --> 00:09:09,300
Fine, fine.

155
00:09:09,660 --> 00:09:13,257
I hereby swear on my
Fluctlight and all the

156
00:09:13,340 --> 00:09:15,900
precious data I've accumulated up to now.

157
00:09:16,220 --> 00:09:21,380
After I've killed you, little one, I shall
allow those three to escape unharmed.

158
00:09:21,560 --> 00:09:22,560
You had better.

159
00:09:30,740 --> 00:09:32,200
I am sorry.

160
00:09:35,540 --> 00:09:36,370
Oh.

161
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:55,940
Was that your best?

162
00:09:56,340 --> 00:09:58,700
Fire all you want, I...

163
00:10:09,200 --> 00:10:11,620
I'm holding back for now, little one.

164
00:10:11,880 --> 00:10:15,257
After all, what fun would it
be if I dispatched you quickly?

165
00:10:15,340 --> 00:10:18,760
I have been waiting 200
years for this moment!

166
00:10:38,420 --> 00:10:41,220
I can't!

167
00:10:41,760 --> 00:10:42,590
Stay back!

168
00:10:46,760 --> 00:10:47,590
What's that?

169
00:10:47,673 --> 00:10:49,060
I can't help.

170
00:10:49,500 --> 00:10:52,540
All I can do is stand here. Powerless.

171
00:10:54,460 --> 00:10:55,290
Thank.

172
00:10:55,600 --> 00:10:57,900
There has to be something I can do.

173
00:10:58,300 --> 00:11:02,560
Instead of whining about being
weak, find a way to fight back.

174
00:11:03,340 --> 00:11:06,660
Now, to finish our centuries-long game.

175
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:08,820
Farewell, dear Lycerin.

176
00:11:09,100 --> 00:11:11,160
Farewell, my only daughter.

177
00:11:11,940 --> 00:11:14,960
Farewell, my other self!

178
00:11:34,180 --> 00:11:35,480
I'm sorry.

179
00:11:35,980 --> 00:11:37,080
I'm so sorry.

180
00:11:37,460 --> 00:11:40,100
No need to apologize.

181
00:11:40,760 --> 00:11:46,680
You still have a mission
to fulfill, don't you?

182
00:11:47,060 --> 00:11:52,900
The three of you will save this
world fragile and beautiful.

183
00:11:53,680 --> 00:11:55,600
We will, no matter what.

184
00:11:57,060 --> 00:11:59,520
You have given me a second chance.

185
00:12:00,520 --> 00:12:03,400
And I shall use it to defend this world.

186
00:12:12,560 --> 00:12:13,440
You two!

187
00:12:21,560 --> 00:12:22,390
That's it.

188
00:12:22,473 --> 00:12:24,060
I finally figured it out.

189
00:12:24,300 --> 00:12:26,712
I know what my purpose is supposed to be.

190
00:12:27,620 --> 00:12:29,260
I'm not going to run away.

191
00:12:29,800 --> 00:12:32,040
I'm going to stay and fulfill my duty.

192
00:12:35,480 --> 00:12:36,580
Please, Cardinal.

193
00:12:37,120 --> 00:12:42,420
With whatever strength you have left,
I want you to turn me into a sword.

194
00:12:44,320 --> 00:12:45,760
Just like her puppet.

195
00:12:54,540 --> 00:12:57,360
Yuji-ho, you can't...

196
00:12:57,900 --> 00:13:03,140
Even if she lets us go, Administrator will
still change half the people into golems.

197
00:13:03,380 --> 00:13:05,380
We can't let her do that to them.

198
00:13:07,700 --> 00:13:10,320
If there's any chance left to stop her,

199
00:13:10,780 --> 00:13:15,000
any hope left at all, this
sacred art must be it.

200
00:13:16,280 --> 00:13:17,417
System call.

201
00:13:17,500 --> 00:13:19,900
Remove core protection.

202
00:13:28,800 --> 00:13:30,077
Go ahead now.

203
00:13:30,160 --> 00:13:31,137
Change me.

204
00:13:31,220 --> 00:13:33,957
The bond between us is strong.

205
00:13:34,040 --> 00:13:37,737
Much stronger than her and
that monster's. Stop it.

206
00:13:37,820 --> 00:13:39,017
Don't do this.

207
00:13:39,100 --> 00:13:40,157
It's okay.

208
00:13:40,240 --> 00:13:43,120
This is what I was meant to do.

209
00:13:53,700 --> 00:13:55,360
Very well, Ugeo.

210
00:13:55,720 --> 00:14:01,180
The final art I cast in life
will go toward your objective.

211
00:14:03,900 --> 00:14:04,780
Hold on.

212
00:14:05,020 --> 00:14:07,785
Before I go, I need to
tell you one last thing.

213
00:14:08,600 --> 00:14:11,040
Metal weapons don't work on the Pontifex,

214
00:14:11,260 --> 00:14:13,966
that's why I couldn't
stab her with my dagger.

215
00:14:44,340 --> 00:14:45,240
Now what?

216
00:14:54,300 --> 00:14:56,117
What do you think you're doing?

217
00:14:56,200 --> 00:14:58,600
Would you die already? No, you don't!

218
00:15:04,820 --> 00:15:07,017
Your lightning will not work on me!

219
00:15:07,100 --> 00:15:08,820
You insolent little knight!

220
00:15:09,060 --> 00:15:10,820
How dare you defy me!

221
00:15:13,240 --> 00:15:16,140
I shall burn all three of you to cinders!

222
00:15:18,380 --> 00:15:20,340
And I shall stop you again!

223
00:15:51,140 --> 00:15:52,500
Release, recollection.

224
00:16:01,580 --> 00:16:03,920
You can mimic my spell, fool.

225
00:16:04,620 --> 00:16:09,720
However, one paltry sword is no match
against my Golem of Thirty Blades!

226
00:16:10,020 --> 00:16:12,600
It will snap it in half
with a single blow!

227
00:16:29,680 --> 00:16:33,520
Human love, beautiful,

228
00:16:33,960 --> 00:16:38,660
the shining light of
purpose, so beautiful.

229
00:16:39,680 --> 00:16:42,340
Yeah, it is.

230
00:16:42,600 --> 00:16:45,760
Kirito, I must go now.

231
00:16:46,280 --> 00:16:49,560
Protect this world and its people.

232
00:16:50,600 --> 00:16:52,900
I leave it to you.

233
00:17:33,880 --> 00:17:34,710
Pucho.

234
00:17:37,020 --> 00:17:37,920
Well, well.

235
00:17:38,760 --> 00:17:41,113
You want to fight some more, little boy?

236
00:17:41,580 --> 00:17:44,277
Do not make the mistake
of becoming overconfident

237
00:17:44,360 --> 00:17:46,660
just because you demolished my puppet.

238
00:17:49,980 --> 00:17:51,160
Don't do it.

239
00:17:52,240 --> 00:17:53,220
Don't go.

240
00:17:54,360 --> 00:17:55,190
Yu-Gi-Oh!

241
00:17:58,120 --> 00:17:59,380
Yu-Gi-Oh!

242
00:17:59,840 --> 00:18:05,840
Yu-Gi-Oh!

243
00:18:10,860 --> 00:18:11,880
Richard Craig!

244
00:18:43,080 --> 00:18:44,920
Oh, my God.

245
00:19:17,520 --> 00:19:19,580
I did not see that coming.

246
00:19:21,020 --> 00:19:23,120
In terms of priority level,

247
00:19:23,380 --> 00:19:28,140
the sword that fused with Eugeo was no
match for my blade, the Silvery Eternity.

248
00:19:28,680 --> 00:19:32,100
But I did not realize his
sword was not metallic.

249
00:19:33,620 --> 00:19:35,240
That was my mistake.

250
00:19:41,080 --> 00:19:42,180
What a bother.

251
00:19:43,200 --> 00:19:45,729
So, it seems you are
the last one standing.

252
00:19:46,200 --> 00:19:49,137
Surprising, to say the least,
boy from the other side.

253
00:19:49,220 --> 00:19:53,700
I am still curious as to why you're
here without administrator privileges.

254
00:19:54,480 --> 00:19:56,951
Although at this point, it doesn't matter.

255
00:20:02,800 --> 00:20:05,540
Now the fight is over, I'm sleepy.

256
00:20:05,960 --> 00:20:09,157
I'll ask the other boy from the
outer world why you were here,

257
00:20:09,240 --> 00:20:12,580
after I fill my chamber
with your blood and screams.

258
00:20:16,540 --> 00:20:18,800
This is the end, boy.

259
00:20:20,200 --> 00:20:23,760
Perhaps we will meet again
someday on the other side.

260
00:20:30,940 --> 00:20:32,600
It's happening again.

261
00:20:37,480 --> 00:20:39,660
I'm letting it happen again.

262
00:20:41,320 --> 00:20:43,497
You do not have to win all the time!

263
00:20:43,580 --> 00:20:46,440
And if you lose, what does it even matter?

264
00:20:46,760 --> 00:20:50,897
In the end, what does is that your
heart and will are remembered.

265
00:20:50,980 --> 00:20:54,397
I am certain everyone
who has spent time with

266
00:20:54,480 --> 00:20:57,560
you and moved on to other
planes believed that,

267
00:20:57,880 --> 00:20:58,757
as do I.

268
00:20:58,840 --> 00:21:01,577
We have given you the strength to stand.

269
00:21:01,660 --> 00:21:06,240
So stand and protect those you hold dear.

270
00:21:28,580 --> 00:21:31,640
Well, now, you can move, can't you?

271
00:21:33,800 --> 00:21:35,660
Yeah, I can take it from here.

272
00:21:37,060 --> 00:21:39,060
If you wish, have had it.

273
00:21:45,120 --> 00:21:46,920
You fought hard, Alice.

274
00:21:47,220 --> 00:21:48,600
And now it's my turn.

275
00:21:49,700 --> 00:21:52,320
Charlotte, Cardinal, and Jujo.

276
00:21:52,520 --> 00:21:54,360
They gave their lives for mine.

277
00:21:54,880 --> 00:21:56,620
Now I'll give mine for yours.

278
00:22:01,660 --> 00:22:02,490
Love you.

279
00:22:06,080 --> 00:22:07,737
Don't try to meet you.

280
00:22:07,820 --> 00:22:08,717
It's the kind of the moment.

281
00:22:08,800 --> 00:22:11,677
You can see the bright blue light.

282
00:22:11,760 --> 00:22:13,140
You can see the truth.

283
00:22:21,260 --> 00:22:24,420
You can't see the voice of the voice.

284
00:22:25,880 --> 00:22:28,757
Don't let anyone know who won't be.

285
00:22:28,840 --> 00:22:30,193
You can't see the rule.

286
00:22:46,100 --> 00:22:47,417
Thank

287
00:22:47,500 --> 00:22:48,817
you

288
00:22:48,900 --> 00:22:55,900
so

289
00:22:58,780 --> 00:23:00,120
much for watching.

290
00:23:34,480 --> 00:23:38,140
Next time, my hero?
